{"task_id": "HumanEval/43", "solution": "def pairs_sum_to_zero(l):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if there are two distinct elements in the list that sum to zero.\n    Uses a set for O(n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen_numbers = set()\n    for num in l:\n        complement = -num\n        if complement in seen_numbers:\n            return True\n        seen_numbers.add(num)\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    res = \"\"\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        res = str(remainder) + res\n        x //= base\n    return res"}
